  "answer_text": "**wakehealth.edu** is the official website of **Atrium Health Wake Forest Baptist**. Based in Winston-Salem, North Carolina, it is a prominent, nationally recognized academic medical center and health system. \n\nThe health system is affiliated with the **Wake Forest University School of Medicine** and is part of **Advocate Health**, one of the largest non-profit health systems in the United States.\n\n### Key Features of the Website\nPatients, students, and healthcare professionals use the website to access a wide range of services:\n\n*   **Patient Portal (MyAtriumHealth):** This is the online hub where patients can log into their accounts to view lab results, message their doctors, pay medical bills, request prescription refills, and manage medical records. \n*   **Find a Doctor & Schedule Appointments:** Users can search for primary care doctors, specialists, pediatricians, and other providers, as well as schedule appointments online.\n*   **Location Directory:** The site provides addresses, contact details, and directions for its emergency departments, urgent care centers, specialized clinics, and regional hospitals across North Carolina.\n*   **Wake Forest University School of Medicine:** The website acts as a gateway for medical students, residents, and researchers looking for information on academic programs, clinical trials, and scientific research initiatives.\n\nIf you are looking for specific medical services, trying to access your patient portal, or seeking academic resources, you can visit the live site at **[wakehealth.edu](https://www.wakehealth.edu)**.",
